From b4f52f8d10692948e31f84171d9c944d9f541fb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neil Johnson <neil.johnson71@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:37:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/26] s19os9: do not close the input file twice

s19os9 aborts as it exits.  On glibc:

    free(): double free detected in tcache 2
    Aborted (core dumped)

exiting 134 rather than 0, even on a run that did everything asked
of it.

nxtline() closes the input file when fgets() reaches the end of it
but leaves inpfp pointing at the closed stream:

	if (fgets(ib, NINPUT, inpfp) == NULL) {
		fclose(inpfp);
		return (0);
	}

asexit() then closes whatever inpfp still points at:

	if (inpfp != NULL) fclose(inpfp);

The guard is there to close the file only if it is open, but
nothing ever tells it the file was closed, so it closes it a second
time.  AddressSanitizer reports the second fclose() through
_IO_new_fclose from asexit() at s19os9.c:554.

Reading a whole input file is the normal path, so this happens on
every successful run.  The damage is confined to the exit status:
the abort is raised inside the C library's cleanup, after the
output file has been closed and its contents are complete, which is
why the fault has gone unnoticed - the .bin it produces is correct.
It is still worth fixing, because a caller that checks the exit
status of s19os9 sees every successful translation as a failure.

Clear inpfp when nxtline() closes it, so the guard in asexit() can
do what it was written to do.  inpfp is not read anywhere between
that point and asexit();  the only other uses are the fopen() that
sets it and the fgets() in nxtline() itself, which is not reached
again once it has returned 0.

Verified:
- Translated s19os9/module.asm, assembled with as6809 and linked to
  Motorola S records:  exits 0, where before it exited 134.  The
  output is byte identical to that of a build from the pristine
  903242b sources, so the translation itself is unchanged.
- Built with -fsanitize=address,undefined and reran:  no reports,
  where before there was a double-free report.
- Checked the exit status on the paths that do not read to end of
  file, which were already correct and remain so:  no arguments
  exits 1, an input file that cannot be opened exits 3.
- Compiled with -Wall with no warnings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 s19os9/s19os9.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/s19os9/s19os9.c b/s19os9/s19os9.c
index aa8956b..fe64c2c 100644
--- a/s19os9/s19os9.c
+++ b/s19os9/s19os9.c
@@ -468,6 +468,7 @@ nxtline(void)
 {
 	if (fgets(ib, NINPUT, inpfp) == NULL) {
 		fclose(inpfp);
+		inpfp = NULL;
 		return (0);
 	}
 	chopcrlf(ib);
